  "_commit": {
    "id": "5cd905c768b96724cd4907bebfc1816001135db4",
    "author": "Gordon Smyth <smyth@wehi.edu.au>",
    "committer": "Gordon Smyth <smyth@wehi.edu.au>",
    "message": "edgeR 4.9.2\n- glmQLFit() with legacy=FALSE now caps any preset dispersions to be <= 4. Previously, large preset dispersions could lead to a segmentation error.\n- glmQLFit() with legacy=FALSE no longer automatically estimates the NB dispersion from trended values found in the DGEList object, if present. The results will now be the same whether the DGEList contains dispersion estimates or not.\n- Adding DTE and DTU references to intro.Rmd.\n- Revise example code for sampleWeights.Rd.\n",
    "time": 1766470174
  },
